OL,2,V55555555CLOCKERBIE: ASHDOWN
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CWARNS OF COVER-UP
OL,5, The Lockerbie disaster demanded a new
OL,6, Govt approach if a personal tragedy was
OL,7, not also to become an international
OL,8, cover-up, Mr Paddy Ashdown said.
OL,10, The Democrats' leader said the criminal
OL,11, inquiry must be carried out with all
OL,12, vigour without "misleading leaks about
OL,13, arrests from Government sources".
OL,15, Transport Secretary Paul Channon "must
OL,16, come clean on all the circumstances
OL,17, surrounding the advance warning".
OL,19, Unless Mr Channon told the Commons
OL,20, every detail as soon as possible calls
OL,21, on both sides of the Atlantic for an
OL,22, official inquiry would be irresistable.
OL,23,F]DFrom 19-03-89 / teletextarchive.com
